author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "The output-budget gate compares measured command output against the contract-declared default_max_estimated_tokens, not against a self-recorded byte snapshot; The gate corpus is measured against a workspace large enough that an unbounded surface exceeds its ceiling, and it includes activity, deps, graph, duplicates, events and bare health; A negative control proves the gate fails when a command is deliberately made unbounded, so a passing run carries information; The output-budget gate runs on every pull request, not only in nightly and release; The help and contracts payload baseline stays a separate declared measurement so discovery cost and answer cost are never conflated; Documentation states which gate owns discovery cost and which owns answer cost, and neither claims the other's coverage"
